nu.tar.gz` | `crypto`, `ic`, `ecbench`, `curve_cover_check`, `hyperelliptic-cover` — glibc |\n| `crypto-*-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz` | same five executables — static |\n| `crypto-*-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz` | same five executables — Apple silicon |\n| `crypto-*-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip` | same five executables (`.exe`) |\n| `isogeny-*-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu.tar.gz` | dedicated `isogeny` executable, README, BUILD.json — glibc |\n| `isogeny-*-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz` | dedicated tool — static |\n| `isogeny-*-aarch64-apple-darwin.tar.gz` | dedicated tool — Apple silicon |\n| `isogeny-*-x86_64-pc-windows-msvc.zip` | dedicated `isogeny.exe` tool |\n| `ecc2k130-cpu-*.tar.gz` | ECC2K-130 client, CPU (`-march=x86-64-v3`) |\n| `ecc2k130-cuda-*.tar.gz` | ECC2K-130 client, CUDA fatbinary (sm_80–sm_120) |\n\nVerify with `sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS`.\n\nRun `isogeny --help` after extracting the dedicated tool archive.\n`isogeny search --curve p224 --ell 1471 --out p224-1471` constructs\nand independently verifies the recorded one-eigenline map.\n\nThe CUDA binary is compiled, not GPU-tested: GitHub runners have no GPU.\n\nBuilt from commit 3714752ee6a9686e0fce79cb308423d9fd09cde9.\n","isDraft":false,"isPrerelease":false,"publishedAt":"2026-10-16T08:54:06Z","tagName":"v0.1.2372","url":"https://github.com/aburan28/crypto/releases/tag/v0.1.2372"}
